nodecode-ttsbuddy is a rewrite of ngelik's ngelik/ttsbuddy-cli:

  https://github.com/ngelik/ttsbuddy-cli
  commit cb7af8ab874ab4643041a12cb6723c24ea787a66
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 ngelik (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the speech provider as a tool that talks to the API the CLI talked
to -- POST https://www.ttsbuddy.com/v1/agent-tts with the text, voice, speed
and language, a bearer key and an Idempotency-Key header (internal/api's
Speak and SpeakRequest), the job poll at GET the same URL with ?id= and its
202/processing/completed/failed/expired states with retry_after_seconds
(cmd/speak.go's handleSpeakResponse and pollUntilComplete), and the download
of the finished MP3 from audio_url with the host allow-list the CLI applied
(internal/api's ValidateDownloadURL: https to the API host or *.amazonaws.com,
http only to loopback). The offline curated voice catalogue -- the Kokoro ids,
names, genders and languages and the ten Supertonic st_* voices
(internal/api/voices.go's CuratedVoices) -- is the cell's data, so the voice
picker costs no request, and the 0.5 to 1.5 accepted speed range is its
(types.go's AcceptedSpeedMin and AcceptedSpeedMax). Exact-job recovery is the
plugin's ttsbuddy_recover tool: GET one known job by id and download it to a
fresh path, never submitting speech again. The settings the plugin held per
profile -- the TTSBUDDY_API_KEY secret, the voice, speed, Supertonic language
and poll timeout -- are the cell's ttsbuddy config section.

Left out: the TTS Buddy CLI itself and everything only it did -- the browser
and email sign-in, the local config and job state under cli_config_dir, the
`hermes ttsbuddy account delete start|confirm|status|cancel` account deletion
with its emailed code, and the CLI's terminal rendering -- because a cell
speaks to the API directly and has no terminal of its own. Also left out:
registration as Hermes' own TTS provider and the voice-bubble conversion
Hermes did after synthesis, since a cell hands the model a file path instead;
and the per-language display names the CLI expanded the ten Supertonic voices
into, so those ten are listed once each and the section's language chooses
the accent.
